  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47dfde0e-4d16-4b72-8282-c9c124962543"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e72ef8bf-f51d-42be-b872-4bb942838a5c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A word too short to be cut in two, or one whose cuts all cancel, has \
co-bracket ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "98e32e35-20aa-4573-bc9a-46aecaa0cdcf"],
 ". Over the alphabet of the circle the first nonzero co-bracket is in length \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e8f123b-f77e-4cd1-a40c-acb7128be22f"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b0018728-8480-42f8-a9ed-a1b0f5174a1e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the second form the co-bracket is applied to each factor of ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " in turn, with the Koszul sign of the shuffle that brings it to the front, \
and the other factors are carried along. The extension raises the number of \
factors by one."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9ec36185-512c-45c1-bde6-6bb43701e929"],

Cell["\<\
Both forms are linear: they distribute over sums and pull out scalars.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3d80de3b-359d-41ca-923c-97a65598bb55"],

Cell["A word may be given as the list of its particles.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5e25edbb-504d-4be3-9fb0-a516dfbe6dae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A product whose head disagrees with the convention of ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 " returns unevaluated."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b8a3a102-c7ce-4a17-bea1-a30d98b9204e"],

